# Task 3: Compare Join Types

## INNER JOIN

Returns only records where a matching customer and order exist.

```sql
SELECT 
    c.customer_id,
    o.order_id,
    o.order_amount
FROM customers c
INNER JOIN orders o
    ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id;
```

## LEFT JOIN

Returns all customers and matching orders where available.

```sql
SELECT 
    c.customer_id,
    o.order_id,
    o.order_amount
FROM customers c
LEFT JOIN orders o
    ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id;
```

## FULL OUTER JOIN

Returns all matching and unmatched records from both tables.

```sql
SELECT 
    c.customer_id,
    o.order_id,
    o.order_amount
FROM customers c
FULL OUTER JOIN orders o
    ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id;
```

## Python Comparison

```python
inner = pd.read_sql(
    """
    SELECT c.customer_id, o.order_id, o.order_amount
    FROM customers c
    INNER JOIN orders o
        ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id
    """,
    engine
)

left = pd.read_sql(
    """
    SELECT c.customer_id, o.order_id, o.order_amount
    FROM customers c
    LEFT JOIN orders o
        ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id
    """,
    engine
)

full = pd.read_sql(
    """
    SELECT c.customer_id, o.order_id, o.order_amount
    FROM customers c
    FULL OUTER JOIN orders o
        ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id
    """,
    engine
)

print(f"INNER: {len(inner)} rows")
print(f"LEFT:  {len(left)} rows")
print(f"FULL:  {len(full)} rows")

assert len(left) >= len(inner)
assert len(full) >= len(inner)

print("Join relationship validation completed.")
```

## Join Comparison

| Join Type       | Records Returned                                |
| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| INNER JOIN      | Only matching records                           |
| LEFT JOIN       | All left-table records + matching right records |
| FULL OUTER JOIN | All records from both tables                    |

